          equipment: "Standard deck, paper and pen for tracking 'Kots'.",
          dealing: 'Dealer deals a batch of 5 cards to each player. After trump selection, the remaining cards are dealt in batches of 4. Play is anticlockwise.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Collect the four tens (Dehlas) to win the hand. Winning all four tens or winning seven consecutive hands results in a 'Kot' (Coat), the ultimate scoring unit.",
          gameplay: "1. Trump Selection: Usually 'First Unable to Follow Suit' (the first time a player can't follow, the card they play sets the trump suit) or 'Eldest Hand' choice.\n2. Double Sar Mechanic: Tricks are not picked up immediately. They accumulate in the center. A player must win two consecutive tricks to pick up the pile.\n3. Breaking the Sar: If the leads change between players of different teams, the pile grows until someone wins two in a row.\n4. Final Trick: The winner of the 13th trick picks up all remaining cards in the center, regardless of the consecutive win rule.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible.',
            "Winning two consecutive tricks is mandatory to collect the center pile ('Double Sar').",
            "If a team wins all four tens, it's a 'Kot'.",
            "Winning 7 consecutive hands is also a 'Kot'.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize winning your second consecutive trick to collect the center pile, especially if it contains a ten.',
          intermediate: "Throw low cards when you know you can't win the second trick of a sequence to avoid helping opponents collect the pile.",
          advanced: "Coordinate with your partner to 'block' opponents' second wins and 'pass' the lead to your partner if they have a stronger follow-up.",
          tips: [
            'Memorize which tens have been played and who collected them.',
            'The last trick is crucial because it captures everything left in the center.',
            "Effective trump management is key to stopping 'Double Sar' sequences.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
